  "evaluation": "A is best: it identifies population as the main difference, appropriately lists outcome measurement and design as additional differences, and explicitly notes that Study B does not establish a harmful direction. B is nearly equivalent, but its suggestion of an extraction artifact is more speculative, and the key direction caveat is less clearly preserved in its detail. C reaches the same defensible classification but introduces an unsupported description of Study A participants as outpatients. All three appropriately avoid treating different depression instruments or populations as grounds for an apparent verdict, though the claimed conflict remains uncertain because Study B's direction is unstated.",
  "ranking": ["A", "B", "C"]
}
